Methods and code followed (also credited in the docstrings of the files named)
--------------------------------------------------------------------------
  AMP: Adversarial Motion Priors, Peng et al., ACM TOG 2021 (the AMP agent is MimicKit's).
  FairGrad, Ban and Ji, 2024. The SciPy least-squares fallback in toppo.py follows the
    formulation of https://github.com/OptMN-Lab/FairGrad (methods/weight_methods.py),
    MIT License, Copyright (c) 2024 OptMN-Lab.
  ARS: Adaptive Reward Scaling, Cho et al., ICML 2025. sac_agent.py reimplements its
    reward-scale rule and learner reset in PyTorch for the AMP reward components; reference
    implementation https://github.com/ms-cho/Adaptive-Reward-Scaling-ARS-for-MTRL (MIT).
  Reward normalization in w5_norm.py follows the update order of VecNormalize in
    https://github.com/openai/baselines (MIT License, Copyright (c) 2017 OpenAI).
  Return-based scaling: Schaul et al., 2021 (arXiv:2105.05347).
  HL-Gauss: Farebrother et al., 2024 (arXiv:2403.03950).
  PCGrad: Yu et al., 2020. PopArt: van Hasselt et al., 2016; Hessel et al., 2019.

